This parameter is required.', example='what can you do?', position='Query'),
  messageType?: string(name='MessageType', description='The message type. Default value: `[primary]`.  

- For regular interactions with the Agent, set the message type to `[primary]`.

- When the message is a response to the Agent\\\\"s Human-in-Loop question, set the type to `[additional]`.

- When the message is intended to trigger report generation, set the type to `[report]`.

- When the message is intended to cancel the current session, set the type to `[cancel]`.', example='primary', position='Query'),
  parentSessionId?: string(name='ParentSessionId', description='The parent session ID.', example='20qrliuoo7p2vlsfg*****', position='Query'),
  question?: string(name='Question', description='This field is required when the message type is `additional`. Specify the specific question that the Agent asks the user through Human-in-Loop.', example='Provide the criteria for calculating GMV', position='Query'),
  quotedMessage?: string(name='QuotedMessage', description='The quoted content. This is typically used during interactions with the Agent.', example='{"version":"v0"}', position='Query'),
  replyTo?: string(name='ReplyTo', description='**Important**

When this message is a reply to an Agent message (for example, the Agent asks a clarifying question through ASK_HUMAN), set reply_to to the exact Checkpoint sequence number carried in that Agent message. If this message is not a targeted reply, such as requesting the Agent to perform further in-depth analysis after analysis is complete, you can leave reply_to empty or set it to "0".  

This field affects how the Agent decides to process the message. Incorrect values may lead to analysis results that do not meet expectations.', example='0', position='Query'),
  sessionConfig?: {
    customAgentId?: string(name='CustomAgentId', description='The custom agent ID. A custom agent is an entity used to customize the analysis process. You can create one in the DataAgent console or by calling the CreateCustomAgent operation. The custom agent ID is a string that starts with `ca-`.', example='ca-asfkjhqwe***aesrfqa'),
    customAgentStage?: string(name='CustomAgentStage', description='The stage of the custom agent.', example='null'),
    enableSearch?: boolean(name='EnableSearch', description='Specifies whether to enable web search.', example='false'),
    kbUuidList?: [ string ](name='KbUuidList', description='The list of knowledge base IDs.', example='dasd***cc211'),
    language?: string(name='Language', description='Currently only Chinese and English are supported. The default value is Chinese. Only uppercase values are supported.', example='ENGLISH'),
    mcpServerIds?: [ string ](name='McpServerIds', description='The MCP server IDs in the session configuration.', example='2q1tu90**********6uttu2nw'),
    mode?: string(name='Mode', description='The mode. Valid values:
 - **ASK_DATA**: data query mode.
 - **ANALYSIS**: analysis mode.
 - **INSIGHT**: insight mode.', example='ANALYSIS'),
    permissionConfig?: {
      defaultAction?: string(name='DefaultAction', description='The default action for table-level permissions. This parameter controls whether tables that are not configured in DataSources.[item].Permission can be queried. Valid values: allow, deny.

- allow (default): works in blacklist mode. By default, all tables can be queried, and the actual permissions are subject to the permissions configured on the Data Management side. Row-level and column-level permissions are enforced only when you configure **row-level and column-level** permissions in DataSources.[item].Permission.

- deny (must be manually specified): works in whitelist mode. By default, no tables can be queried. A table can be queried only when you configure permissions for it in DataSources.[item].Permission. You can grant full access to a table by not configuring any row-level or column-level restrictions.', example='allow'),
    }(name='PermissionConfig', description='The session level data permission settings. If this parameter is set multiple times across multiple turns within the same session, the last setting takes effect.'),
    planMode?: string(name='PlanMode', description='Specifies whether to enable the plan. Valid values: disable, enable, force. Default value: enable.', example='disable'),
    reportWaterMark?: string(name='ReportWaterMark', description='The text of up to 64 characters that is used as a watermark in the generated PDF report.', example='sample-watermark'),
    skipAskHuman?: boolean(name='SkipAskHuman', description='Specifies whether to disable user inquiries during the process.', example='True'),
    skipPlan?: boolean(name='SkipPlan', description='Specifies whether to skip the plan confirmation step.', example='True'),
    skipSqlConfirm?: boolean(name='SkipSqlConfirm', description='Specifies whether to skip all SQL confirmations.', example='False'),
    skipWebReportConfirm?: boolean(name='SkipWebReportConfirm', description='Specifies whether to skip the web report generation confirmation.', example='True'),
    userSpecifiedSkillList?: [ string ](name='UserSpecifiedSkillList', description='The list of user-specified skills.'),
  }(name='SessionConfig', description='The special configuration for the current session. For the same session, only the configuration included in the first SendMessage call takes effect.', shrink='json', position='Query'),
  sessionId?: string(name='SessionId', description='The session ID. This is an optional field used for multi-turn sessions.
- You can start a session without specifying this field. The response includes the SessionID of the current session.
- You can also manually create a session ID by calling the CreateDataAgentSession operation and include the ID when initiating a session.
- For multi-turn conversations (such as follow-up questions or confirming execution plans), specify the SessionID returned by the previous SendChatMessage call.', example='sess_***', position='Query'),
  taskConfig?: {
    reportConfig?: {
      reportPrompt?: string(name='ReportPrompt', description='The prompt that the report must follow.', example='generate a report'),
      reportTheme?: string(name='ReportTheme', description='The report theme. Valid values: default, journal, legacy, and neobrutalism.', example='default'),
      reportType?: string(name='ReportType', description='The service type. Valid values: TextReport and WebReport, which indicate that the task generates a text report or a web report. Currently, only WebReport is supported.', example='WebReport'),
    }(name='ReportConfig', description='The configuration of the report rule. Only when MesageType is set to REPORT, a report task is executed based on this configuration.'),
  }(name='TaskConfig', description='The configuration items that affect only the current task.', shrink='json', position='Query'),
  userOssBucket?: string(name='UserOssBucket', description='The OSS bucket of the user. If this parameter is not specified, the analysis data is securely stored in built-in storage.', example='my-bucket', position='Query'),
  workspaceId?: string(name='WorkspaceId', description='The workspace ID.', example='c1p71ne***baexrt3o', position='Query'),
}

